    "kind": "good",
    "note": "Nucleophilic addition to a carbonyl in its plainest form: attack, then protonation, and the pi pair goes onto oxygen rather than anywhere else. The proton comes from HCN drawn as a member of the multiset, and the cyanide it leaves behind is the same nucleophile the reaction started with, which is what makes HCN and cyanide a buffer pair here rather than two unrelated reagents. Cyanide attacks through carbon; the nitrogen lone pair is present and untouched, so the arrow that was not drawn is visible."
